मण्डलम् उत्सर्जन ॥ ॰ codegen — the port of crates/sadhana/src/t1/regalloc.rs
॰                    and crates/sadhana/src/t1/x86_64.rs (emit.rs: retired
॰                    and deleted, `W-237`)

॰ ══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════
॰ CODE GENERATION, task D-002e, doc 03 §8 — the last slice of the D-002
॰ chain.
॰
॰ It takes what मध्यरूप built — वृत्ति, पर्व and the linear आज्ञाकोश —
॰ decides where every मूल्याङ्क lives, and turns that into text.
॰ Doc 03 §8's phase 3.4 splits the same work three ways and this file is
॰ all three: 3.4.7 the linear-scan register allocator, 3.4.8 T0 emission
॰ for riscv64, and 3.4.11 the x86-64 backend.
॰ RETIRED PAIR, 2026-09-04 (`W-236`, research/25 §1.2): the 3.4.8 claim is
॰ WITHDRAWN — `कार्यक्रमोत्सर्जनम्` and its twin `emit.rs` emit a text that is
॰ NOT T0 (`निधेहि`/`प्रत्यावर्तनम्` are in no mnemonic table, `कोष्ठ५` names no
॰ register the assembler knows, no operand carries a kāraka), so `सङ्केतन`
॰ refuses every line; the T0 emitter is `crates/sadhana/src/t1/riscv64.rs`
॰ with its twin `yantrotsarjana.t1` (यन्त्रोत्सर्जन), and `W-237` deletes the
॰ retired pair. 3.4.7 and 3.4.11 are not retired; do not extend 3.4.8.
॰ DELETED, 2026-09-04 (`W-237`): the three routines of 3.4.8 are gone from
॰ this file and `emit.rs` from the tree — see THE RETIRED T0 PAIR below.
॰
॰ ── WHAT THIS FILE REPLACES, AND WHAT IT ACTUALLY HELD ──
॰ 28 lines of tools/port_encode.py output, and IT WAS NOT THE CODEGEN
॰ THE FILENAME CLAIMS — it was regalloc.rs's two types and nothing else.
॰ Not one symbol of emit.rs or x86_64.rs appeared in it: no
॰ emit_program, no X86_64Emitter, no reg_name. Two thirds of the module
॰ were absent and the file gave no sign of it.
॰ It also INVENTED, exactly as ir.t1's predecessor did:
॰   • लओकएशअनएएनटरय — "LocationEntry". `grep -r LocationEntry` returns
॰     ZERO hits in any Rust source in this tree. regalloc.rs writes
॰     `HashMap<ValueId, Location>` and names no entry struct.
॰   • उतसरजन — a routine taking (ir.Function, AllocationMap) and
॰     returning `सम्भाव्य अङ्कः अन्तः अ८`. NOTHING in regalloc.rs,
॰     emit.rs or x86_64.rs returns bytes; both emitters return text.
॰ And it split `enum Location` into a गणना plus a संरचना without saying
॰ so, which is the right shape for T1 but was arrived at by accident.
॰ The generator now refuses to run. Every line below is hand-written
॰ from the three Rust files named at the top.
॰
॰ ── ON THE MODULE NAME ── doc 03 §2's component table names the codegen
॰ रूपकार (rūpakāra), *"codegen → T0 text"*. spec/marks.tsv has NO row
॰ for this module at all — it names विश्लेषणम् the disassembler and कोशः
॰ the object format and stops. The name kept here is उत्सर्जन, for one
॰ reason only: ir.t1 line 8 already says *"for उत्सर्जन (D-002e) to
॰ allocate registers over"*, so the sibling that feeds this module has
॰ committed to the word, and ir.t1 is not this row's file to edit.
॰ THE DISAGREEMENT IS RECORDED RATHER THAN SILENTLY DECIDED: if रूपकार
॰ wins, it is one rename here and one line in ir.t1, and doc 03 §2 is
॰ the authority that should settle it.
॰
॰ ── ON THE NAMES ── lexicon words where spec/lexicon.src.tsv has one:
॰ कोष्ठ register (attested), आवण्टकः allocator (doc11), मुक्तिः free
॰ (doc11), क्रम order (attested), संख्यानम् count (attested), रेखा line
॰ (doc05). Derived, and each said out loud because none is in the
॰ lexicon: अधिकरण — the locative kāraka, the grammarians' word for the
॰ LOCUS of an action, for Location, the locus a value lives at;
॰ निक्षेप — a deposit, a thing laid down and kept, for Spill;
॰ आयुस् — lifespan, for a live interval; सक्रिय — active.
॰ वचनम् for "the text of" follows encode.t1's सङ्केतनदोषवचनम्.
॰ यवन IS A PLACEHOLDER AND IS FLAGGED: no lexicon row names an
॰ instruction-set architecture, so x86-64's emitter has no attested
॰ name to take. यवन is the classical word for the foreign; a real name
॰ is a row in spec/lexicon.src.tsv that somebody must file, and until
॰ then this one is marked rather than passed off as attested.
॰
॰ ── ON GROUPING ── spec/grammar-t1.ebnf says operators and their
॰ precedence are NOT frozen. Every order-dependent expression below is
॰ bracketed with आरभ्य ॱ समाप्तम्, so the file means one thing under
॰ either eventual rule. मध्यरूप and संयोजन do the same.
॰
॰ ── ON THE ARENAS ── Rust holds HashMap<ValueId,(usize,usize)>,
॰ Vec<(ValueId,Instruction)> and three parallel Vec pushes. T1 has
॰ neither a map nor a growable collection. This file invents nothing:
॰ it adopts the preallocated कोश plus module-level सूचकाङ्क that
॰ व्याकर committed to and मध्यरूप followed. THE MAPS NEED NO SUBSTITUTE
॰ AT ALL — मध्यरूप numbers मूल्याङ्क from a dense 1-based counter, so a
॰ map keyed on ValueId IS an array subscripted by the value number, and
॰ that is how आयुरारम्भकोश, आयुरन्तकोश and अधिकरणकोश are written. The
॰ Vec-of-tuples become parallel arrays, because T1 has no tuple.
॰
॰ ── ON TEXT ── ADR-0017 (docs/adr/0017-a-string-literal-is-a-token.md)
॰ gave T1 a string LITERAL TOKEN: `उक्तम् … इति`, taken by the lexer
॰ before it strips the comment, interior whitespace the source's own,
॰ `॰` inside it ordinary text, a doubled `इति इति` for the word itself.
॰ The three routines below that now build text use it.
॰ NOTHING IN THIS FILE WRITES A `॰` INSIDE A LITERAL, and that is a
॰ decision rather than an oversight: this file is read by lex_t1, where
॰ a `॰` inside a string is text, AND by tests/t1_sources.rs, which
॰ reads every .t1 source with the T0 `lex`, where it still ends the
॰ line. One literal meaning two things to two readers is the exact
॰ defect ADR-0017 was written to remove.
॰
॰ CONCATENATION IS योगः, AND THIS FILE CHOOSES IT OUT LOUD — AND THEN
॰ STOPPED USING IT ON 2026-08-30. The paragraph below is kept because it
॰ is the record of a decision and B-082 still owns the question; what was
॰ found this session is that the decision HAS NO IMPLEMENTATION. `योगः`
॰ on two पाठः answers *"expected a number, found Octets"* in the one
॰ reader that executes T1, so the two routines written on it — देवनागराङ्कः
॰ and अधिकरणवचनम् — could never have been run. They are appenders now.
॰ See THE OUTPUT BUFFER below.
॰ spec/grammar-t1.ebnf freezes no operator at all — "OPERATORS AND
॰ THEIR PRECEDENCE" is its own last open section — so there is no
॰ ratified spelling to take, and two candidates existed:
॰   • अधि, doc 07 §4.2's join and the one crates/sadhana/src/t1/
॰     drishya.rs implements for a view's text_expr. REFUSED, on its own
॰     documented rule: pieces joined by अधि are "separated by exactly
॰     one space". That is right for a view and wrong for assembly,
॰     where every space in the output is the output's own.
॰   • योगः, which व्याकर already reads as an infix operator
॰     (crates/sadhana-t1/src/parse.t1:157 → वास्तुॱयोगद्विकर्मभेद) and
॰     which this file already writes on every arithmetic line. TAKEN:
॰     it coins no word, needs no lexer change, and is the same overload
॰     every language with `+` on strings makes.
॰ WHAT THAT DOES NOT SETTLE IS THE TYPE, and B-082 owns it: nothing in
॰ this tree yet distinguishes योगः on two अ६४ from योगः on two पाठः.
॰ Recorded here rather than left to be discovered there.
॰
॰ ── ON ZERO ── मध्यरूप's arenas are 1-based and ० means ABSENT, and
॰ this file keeps that. ० in आयुरारम्भकोश is `lifetimes.get(v) == None`;
॰ ० in अधिकरण ॱ भेद is `alloc.locations.get(v) == None`, which is the
॰ dead-code test emit.rs makes. ONE PLACE NEEDS AN EXCEPTION AND IT IS
॰ MARKED: register number ० is a real register (x0, %rax), so the free
॰ list cannot use ० for "empty". मुक्तकोष्ठग्रहणम् returns the register
॰ PLUS ONE and ० means the list was empty; its one caller subtracts.
॰
॰ ── WHAT IS PORTED AND WHAT IS NOT ── regalloc.rs is ported whole:
॰ all three of its symbols, and the whole body of allocate_registers,
॰ its CFG flattening, its lifetime pass and its linear scan with the
॰ spill-the-longer-interval rule. Of emit.rs's and x86_64.rs's seven
॰ routines ALL SEVEN ARE NOW REAL, as of 2026-08-30. The last three —
॰ कार्यक्रमोत्सर्जनम्, यवनवृत्त्युत्सर्जनम् and यवनाधिकरणवचनम् — landed
॰ on TWO decisions and no new code in any other file:
॰   • THE NEWLINE. ADR-0017 is NOT amended and a string literal still
॰     holds none. A newline is an OCTET THE EMITTER APPENDS, which is
॰     ADR-0018's own rule; see THE OUTPUT BUFFER below. ADR-0028's
॰     allocator was not needed and is not a prerequisite.
॰   • THE LATIN. ADR-0029 settled the register NAMES; this file settles
॰     `%`, `$`, `(`, `)` and `-` by the same principle one level down,
॰     under HOW AT&T PUNCTUATION IS WRITTEN IN THIS REPERTOIRE. Every
॰     answer there is a citation — C-15-2, the frozen numeral production,
॰     spec/lexicon.src.tsv — and not a coinage, with the ONE exception
॰     that is flagged as a debt: see (e) at the foot.
॰ (b) and (c) at the foot are rewritten to say what cleared them rather
॰ than deleted, because "it works now" and "here is the decision that
॰ made it possible" are different facts.
॰ The ratchet in tests/t1_sources.rs counts emitters with a real body,
॰ because a count of declared symbols and a count of real bodies would
॰ both read as finished while the codegen emitted nothing — and
॰ tests/t1_execution.rs now RUNS all three and asserts the octets,
॰ because a count of real bodies reads as finished while the emitter
॰ writes the wrong text. It also records the finding that stopped those
॰ tests from allocating for real: कोष्ठावण्टनम् cannot be run over a
॰ real function yet. See (f).
॰ ══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════

आयातः मध्यरूप ।

