॰ The block walk of emit_function, split out so the prologue and epilogue
॰ above read as the two halves they are. Same flattening as रेखीकरणम्
॰ and कार्यक्रमोत्सर्जनम् — see (d) at the foot for the absent sort.
सार्वजनिक वृत्तिः यवनपर्वोत्सर्जनम् आदाय वृत्तिसूचकाङ्क ॱॱ न६४ ऽ आवण्टितम् ॱॱ आवण्टनम् ददाति न६४ आदि
    चरः कार्यम् ॱॱ मध्यरूपॱवृत्ति भवति मध्यरूपॱवृत्तिकोश अङ्कः वृत्तिसूचकाङ्क अन्तः ।
    चरः पर्वाङ्कः ॱॱ न६४ भवति कार्यम् ॱ पर्वारम्भ ।
    चरः शेषपर्व ॱॱ न६४ भवति कार्यम् ॱ पर्वसंख्यान ।

    यावत् शेषपर्व अधिकम् ० आदि
        चरः पर्वम् ॱॱ मध्यरूपॱपर्व भवति मध्यरूपॱपर्वकोश अङ्कः पर्वाङ्कः अन्तः ।
        चरः आज्ञाङ्कः ॱॱ न६४ भवति पर्वम् ॱ आज्ञारम्भ ।
        चरः शेषाज्ञा ॱॱ न६४ भवति पर्वम् ॱ आज्ञासंख्यान ।

        यावत् शेषाज्ञा अधिकम् ० आदि
            चरः आदेशः ॱॱ मध्यरूपॱआज्ञा भवति मध्यरूपॱआज्ञाकोश अङ्कः आज्ञाङ्कः अन्तः ।
            चरः फलाङ्कः ॱॱ न६४ भवति आदेशः ॱ फलम् ॱ क्रमाङ्क ।
            चरः लक्ष्यम् ॱॱ अधिकरण भवति अधिकरणग्रहणम् आरभ्य फलाङ्कः ऽ आवण्टितम् ॱ अधिकरणसंख्यान समाप्तम् ।

            यदि लक्ष्यम् ॱ भेद अधिकम् ० आदि
                ॰ Instruction::ConstInt(c) => "  movq ${c}, {rname}\n"
                यदि आदेशः ॱ भेद समम् मध्यरूपॱध्रुवाज्ञाभेद आदि
                    चरः लेखैक ॱॱ न६४ भवति विवरयोजनम् २ ।
                    चरः लेखद्वि ॱॱ न६४ भवति पाठयोजनम् उक्तम् निधेहि इति ।
                    चरः लेखत्रि ॱॱ न६४ भवति विवरयोजनम् १ ।
                    चरः लेखचतुः ॱॱ अङ्कः अन्तः अ८ भवति देवनागराङ्कः आदेशः ॱ ध्रुवमूल्यम् ।
                    चरः लेखपञ्च ॱॱ न६४ भवति विच्छेदयोजनम् ।
                    चरः लेखषट् ॱॱ अङ्कः अन्तः अ८ भवति यवनाधिकरणवचनम् लक्ष्यम् ।
                    चरः लेखसप्त ॱॱ न६४ भवति यतियोजनम् ।
                इति

                ॰ Instruction::Add(v1, v2) — a two-operand ISA, so the
                ॰ destination must already hold the left operand
                यदि आदेशः ॱ भेद समम् मध्यरूपॱयोगाज्ञाभेद आदि
                    चरः वामाधिकरणम् ॱॱ अधिकरण भवति अधिकरणग्रहणम् आरभ्य आदेशः ॱ वाम ॱ क्रमाङ्क ऽ आवण्टितम् ॱ अधिकरणसंख्यान समाप्तम् ।
                    चरः दक्षिणाधिकरणम् ॱॱ अधिकरण भवति अधिकरणग्रहणम् आरभ्य आदेशः ॱ दक्षिण ॱ क्रमाङ्क ऽ आवण्टितम् ॱ अधिकरणसंख्यान समाप्तम् ।

                    ॰ if rn_out != rn1 { "  movq {rn1}, {rn_out}\n" }
                    यदि अधिकरणसाम्यम् आरभ्य लक्ष्यम् ऽ वामाधिकरणम् समाप्तम् समम् ० आदि
                        चरः लेखाष्ट ॱॱ न६४ भवति विवरयोजनम् २ ।
                        चरः लेखनव ॱॱ न६४ भवति पाठयोजनम् उक्तम् निधेहि इति ।
                        चरः लेखदश ॱॱ न६४ भवति विवरयोजनम् १ ।
                        चरः लेखैकादश ॱॱ अङ्कः अन्तः अ८ भवति यवनाधिकरणवचनम् वामाधिकरणम् ।
                        चरः लेखद्वादश ॱॱ न६४ भवति विच्छेदयोजनम् ।
                        चरः लेखत्रयोदश ॱॱ अङ्कः अन्तः अ८ भवति यवनाधिकरणवचनम् लक्ष्यम् ।
                        चरः लेखचतुर्दश ॱॱ न६४ भवति यतियोजनम् ।
                    इति

                    ॰ "  addq {rn2}, {rn_out}\n"
                    चरः लेखपञ्चदश ॱॱ न६४ भवति विवरयोजनम् २ ।
                    चरः लेखषोडश ॱॱ न६४ भवति पाठयोजनम् उक्तम् योगः इति ।
                    चरः लेखसप्तदश ॱॱ न६४ भवति विवरयोजनम् १ ।
                    चरः लेखाष्टादश ॱॱ अङ्कः अन्तः अ८ भवति यवनाधिकरणवचनम् दक्षिणाधिकरणम् ।
                    चरः लेखैकोनविंशति ॱॱ न६४ भवति विच्छेदयोजनम् ।
                    चरः लेखविंशति ॱॱ अङ्कः अन्तः अ८ भवति यवनाधिकरणवचनम् लक्ष्यम् ।
                    चरः लेखैकविंशति ॱॱ न६४ भवति यतियोजनम् ।
                इति

                ॰ Rust's `_ => {}` — genuinely nothing. NOT emit.rs's `_`
                ॰ arm, which writes a comment; x86_64.rs writes no line at
                ॰ all for a Sub, and that difference is ported as it stands.
            इति

            आज्ञाङ्कः भवति आरभ्य आज्ञाङ्कः योगः १ समाप्तम् ।
            शेषाज्ञा भवति आरभ्य शेषाज्ञा वियोगः १ समाप्तम् ।
        इति

        पर्वाङ्कः भवति आरभ्य पर्वाङ्कः योगः १ समाप्तम् ।
        शेषपर्व भवति आरभ्य शेषपर्व वियोगः १ समाप्तम् ।
    इति
    प्रत्यागमनम् निर्गमसूचकाङ्क ।
इति

॰ X86_64Emitter::reg_name(&self, usize) -> &'static str
॰
॰ WRITTEN 2026-08-30, and what unblocked it was a TABLE, not an allocator.
॰ वाक्यविभाग:845 names the blocker these emitters share: "spec/…tsv gains a
॰ Devanagari column, or the shape oracle compares भेद numbers instead of
॰ words. It is the same blocker that holds four of उत्सर्जन's seven
॰ emitters." ADR-0029 settled what the column may contain — Devanagari, no
॰ Latin escape — and spec/registers-amd64.tsv now carries it, so the
॰ condition that note set is met for THIS routine.
॰
॰ THE NAMES ARE ROLES, NOT SOUNDS, and that is ADR-0029 as AMENDED rather
॰ than as first written. registers-riscv64.tsv was already generated with
॰ शून्यः for `zero` and स्तूपसूचकः for `sp`, so one compiler would have
॰ held two register tables spelled by two principles. rax IS the
॰ Accumulator and rcx the Counter; r8-r15 have no role and stay numbers.
॰
॰ RETURNS A SLICE AND NOT पाठः. The stub said पाठः, which is what
॰ यवनाधिकरणवचनम् above needs — Rust's format_location returns an owned
॰ String. reg_name returns &'static str, a BORROW into the binary, and
॰ कारकनाम (वाक्यविभाग:2368) is the same shape already written this way.
॰ An owned string here would need ADR-0028's allocator for nothing.
॰
॰ DIVERGENCE, stated: Rust panics with "out of registers" past 13. This
॰ returns the empty slice, because the allocator hands out 0..13 and never
॰ more (x86_64.rs:118), so the arm is unreachable rather than lenient. A
॰ caller that prints an empty register name has been given an index the
॰ allocator could not have produced.
सार्वजनिक वृत्तिः कोष्ठनाम आदाय कोष्ठाङ्कः ॱॱ न६४ ददाति अङ्कः अन्तः अ८ आदि
    यदि कोष्ठाङ्कः समम् ० आदि प्रत्यागमनम् उक्तम् सञ्चयः इति । इति
    यदि कोष्ठाङ्कः समम् १ आदि प्रत्यागमनम् उक्तम् आधारः इति । इति
    यदि कोष्ठाङ्कः समम् २ आदि प्रत्यागमनम् उक्तम् गणकः इति । इति
    यदि कोष्ठाङ्कः समम् ३ आदि प्रत्यागमनम् उक्तम् दत्तम् इति । इति
    यदि कोष्ठाङ्कः समम् ४ आदि प्रत्यागमनम् उक्तम् मूलाङ्कः इति । इति
    यदि कोष्ठाङ्कः समम् ५ आदि प्रत्यागमनम् उक्तम् लक्ष्याङ्कः इति । इति
    यदि कोष्ठाङ्कः समम् ६ आदि प्रत्यागमनम् उक्तम् कोष्ठ८ इति । इति
    यदि कोष्ठाङ्कः समम् ७ आदि प्रत्यागमनम् उक्तम् कोष्ठ९ इति । इति
    यदि कोष्ठाङ्कः समम् ८ आदि प्रत्यागमनम् उक्तम् कोष्ठ१० इति । इति
    यदि कोष्ठाङ्कः समम् ९ आदि प्रत्यागमनम् उक्तम् कोष्ठ११ इति । इति
    यदि कोष्ठाङ्कः समम् १० आदि प्रत्यागमनम् उक्तम् कोष्ठ१२ इति । इति
    यदि कोष्ठाङ्कः समम् ११ आदि प्रत्यागमनम् उक्तम् कोष्ठ१३ इति । इति
    यदि कोष्ठाङ्कः समम् १२ आदि प्रत्यागमनम् उक्तम् कोष्ठ१४ इति । इति
    यदि कोष्ठाङ्कः समम् १३ आदि प्रत्यागमनम् उक्तम् कोष्ठ१५ इति । इति

    चरः रिक्तम् ॱॱ अङ्कः अन्तः अ८ भवति ० ।
    प्रत्यागमनम् रिक्तम् ।
इति


॰ ══════════════════ what is NOT ported, and why ══════════════════
॰
॰ (a) CLOSED BY `W-236` (2026-09-04), KEPT FOR ir.t1's REASON: its stated
॰     wait was right and is over. It read: "आयुर्निर्णयः HAS NO Call ARM
॰     … there is no fourth arena holding argument value numbers … When it
॰     lands, this arm is six lines and आयुर्विस्तारः is already the body
॰     of them." `W-204` landed the fourth arena, मध्यरूपॱआदानकोश, and the
॰     builder's call arm; the six lines are in आयुर्निर्णयः now. What made
॰     them urgent rather than tidy: the T1 RISC-V emitter (yantrotsarjana
॰     .t1) allocates through कोष्ठावण्टनम् and its text must agree with
॰     riscv64.rs's octet for octet — an argument whose interval ended at
॰     its definition would free its register one instruction early, and
॰     the two twins would name different स्थिरs for the same value.
॰
॰ (b) WHAT BLOCKED THE TWO EMITTERS, AND WHAT CLEARED EACH OF IT.
॰     NOTHING HERE IS OPEN ANY MORE — every numbered item below is
॰     answered, and the note is kept whole because the answers are only
॰     legible beside the questions they closed. It is REWRITTEN rather
॰     than amended each time, on the rule this file follows: a list with
॰     one stale entry teaches the next reader to skip the part that is
॰     still true.
॰
॰     CLEARED, by docs/adr/0017-a-string-literal-is-a-token.md:
॰       1. THE STRING LITERAL TOKEN — the thing the old note correctly
॰          said was "an ADR against spec/grammar-t1.ebnf" and not
॰          something a port could close. It is that ADR. `token` now
॰          lists `string`, crates/sadhana/src/lex.rs `lex_t1` reads it,
॰          and `उक्तम् … इति` is one token where it used to be five.
॰       2. A GROWABLE पाठः — WITHDRAWN, because it was never needed.
॰          `out.push_str(s)` is `out = out योगः s`, and the result of a
॰          concatenation is an EXPRESSION whose growth belongs to the
॰          operator and not to the program. The preallocated कोश this
॰          file uses for every Vec is therefore NOT introduced for
॰          text, and no arena was added. See ON TEXT at the head for
॰          which operator and what B-082 still owes it.
॰       3. FORMATTED INTERPOLATION — WITHDRAWN for the same reason
॰          once (1) and (2) hold: `format!` is a concatenation of
॰          pieces. Its stated bottom, that देवनागराङ्कः "needs a
॰          character literal to map '0' onto '०'", was an artefact of
॰          reading Rust's char-to-char map as the only shape. A digit
॰          taken as a NUMBER and returned as a one-akṣara पाठः needs
॰          no character literal; अङ्कचिह्नम् above is that, in ten
॰          lines.
॰
॰     CLEARED 2026-08-30, AND THE ANSWER WAS NOT THE ONE THIS NOTE
॰     ASKED FOR:
॰       4. A STRING CANNOT HOLD A NEWLINE, AND CANNOT BEGIN OR END
॰          WITH A SPACE. Both are ADR-0017's, in its own *What this
॰          does NOT settle*: a string does not cross a newline, there
॰          is no escape for one, and a leading or trailing space is
॰          "not representable, because the delimiters are words and
॰          words are whitespace-separated". BOTH EMITTERS ARE LINE
॰          ORIENTED — emit_program's eight push_str calls all end in a
॰          newline and six begin with four spaces; emit_function's
॰          twelve do the same — so this is not an inconvenience, it is
॰          the format. **ALL OF THAT IS STILL TRUE, AND NONE OF IT WAS
॰          THE BLOCKER.** This note asked for a successor ADR giving
॰          `उक्तम् … इति` an escape. It did not get one and does not
॰          need one: the owner's decision of 2026-08-30 is that A
॰          NEWLINE IS A BYTE THE EMITTER APPENDS, which is what
॰          ADR-0018 already says — *"a line break is written by the
॰          emitter as a byte, through the routine that appends one, not
॰          smuggled inside quotes"*. The indent is the same answer: a
॰          string that may not BEGIN with a space is not asked to, and
॰          विवरयोजनम् writes four. ADR-0017 is untouched to the letter,
॰          which is the part of this that was worth waiting for.
॰          THE MISTAKE THIS NOTE MADE IS WORTH NAMING, because it cost
॰          the row time: it read "the emitter needs a newline" as "the
॰          STRING needs a newline", and the second does not follow from
॰          the first. A literal is one token; a line is an output.
॰       5. THE AMD64 TEXT IS LATIN — (c), cleared by ADR-0029 and this
॰          file's punctuation decision.
॰
॰ (c) THE LATIN BLOCKER WAS THREE OF x86_64.rs's FOUR ROUTINES, NOT
॰     कोष्ठनाम ALONE — and all three are written as of 2026-08-30.
॰     That count was a correction to this note and it was found the only
॰     way it could be, by writing the ones that could be written and
॰     reading what the other three actually emit:
॰       • कोष्ठनाम returns "rax" … "r15": fourteen names in Latin,
॰         which is what this note already said.
॰       • यवनाधिकरणवचनम् returns `%{name}` and `-{n}(%rbp)`. `%`, `(`,
॰         `)` and `-` are outside the repertoire BEFORE a register
॰         name is reached, so it is blocked even if कोष्ठनाम were not.
॰       • यवनवृत्त्युत्सर्जनम् emits `.globl main`, `main:`,
॰         `pushq %rbp`, `movq %rsp, %rbp`, `movq`, `addq`,
॰         `popq %rbp` and `ret` — GNU as syntax throughout, and
॰         blocked on (b)(4) as well.
॰     WHY THIS IS A BLOCKER HERE AND A RESPELLING IN emit.rs, WHICH IS
॰     THE PART THAT IS NOT ARBITRARY: emit.rs emits T0, AND T0 IS A
॰     DEVANAGARI LANGUAGE. Its `x5`, `a0`, `main` and `;` are Latin
॰     PLACEHOLDERS in a Rust mock — the file's own comment says "We
॰     mock the function name" — standing in for text that
॰     spec/registers-riscv64.tsv and spec/directives.tsv already spell
॰     in Devanagari, so respelling them moves the output TOWARD T0 and
॰     not away from the Rust. x86_64.rs emits assembly for a
॰     Latin-script assembler, where `movq` stands in for nothing:
॰     respelled, it stops being AMD64. ADR-0017 drew this line itself —
॰     "a Latin letter inside `उक्तम् … इति` is refused exactly as it is
॰     anywhere else, which is also why this ADR does not unblock
॰     D-002e's कोष्ठनाम" — and what is new here is only that it falls
॰     in three places.
॰     THE DECISION IS TAKEN, IN TWO PARTS, AND THIS NOTE IS THE RECORD
॰     OF WHERE EACH PART LIVES:
॰       • THE NAMES — docs/adr/0029, 2026-08-30. Devanagari, no Latin
॰         escape, TRANSLATED BY ROLE rather than transcribed by sound,
॰         with spec/registers-amd64.tsv as the table. This note used to
॰         offer "transliterate, or keep the mapping numeric"; the answer
॰         is neither, and it was the tree's rather than the ADR's —
॰         spec/registers-riscv64.tsv was already generated by role
॰         (शून्यः for `zero`), and one compiler with two register tables
॰         spelled by two principles is worse than either principle.
॰         The transliteration this note feared — `रक्स्` for `rax` — is
॰         exactly the एनकओडइनग mistake, and it was refused for that
॰         reason.
॰       • THE PUNCTUATION AND THE MNEMONICS — this file, 2026-08-30, in
॰         HOW AT&T PUNCTUATION IS WRITTEN IN THIS REPERTOIRE above
॰         यवनाधिकरणवचनम्. ADR-0029 said nothing about `%`, `$`, `(`,
॰         `)` or `-`, which this note had correctly found were the
॰         characters that stop the emitter FIRST. Each is answered by a
॰         citation there.
॰     AND THE COST ADR-0029 NAMED IS REAL AND IS NOT SOFTENED HERE: the
॰     emitted text is not consumable by `as` verbatim, and a boundary
॰     pass reading the same TSV in the other direction is what makes it
॰     so. That pass does not exist yet and is not this file's.
॰     यवनोत्सर्जकारम्भः was the one routine of the four the blocker did
॰     not reach, because it emits no target text at all: `String::new()`
॰     is the empty literal.
॰
॰ (d) रेखीकरणम् DOES NOT SORT, and that is deliberate, not missing.
॰     regalloc.rs sorts func.blocks.keys() because a HashMap has no
॰     order; मध्यरूप stores a function's blocks as a contiguous run
॰     appended in id order, so the run is the sorted key list already.
॰     Written out at the head of that routine so the absent sort reads
॰     as a decision rather than an omission.
॰
॰ (e) THE AMD64 BACK END NAMES TWO REGISTERS NO TABLE IN THIS TREE
॰     CARRIES, AND ONE OF THEM IS A DEBT.
॰     spec/registers-amd64.tsv covers the fourteen ALLOCATABLE registers
॰     and says so in its own header: the number column is "the index
॰     `X86_64Emitter::reg_name` matches on … 0..13". emit_function's
॰     prologue and epilogue need TWO MORE, and neither is allocatable:
॰       • `%rsp` → स्तूपसूचकः. NOT A DEBT: spec/lexicon.src.tsv:394 has
॰         the row, glossed `stack pointer`, and spec/registers-riscv64
॰         .tsv:13 already spells `sp` with it. Read, not coined.
॰       • `%rbp` → आधारसूचकः. A DEBT, and it is stated rather than
॰         passed off as attested. No row anywhere in spec/ carries it.
॰         It is DERIVED under the two tables' own rule — `आधारः` is
॰         registers-amd64.tsv's word for the Base and `-सूचकः` is how
॰         स्तूपसूचकः, विश्वसूचकः and तन्तुसूचकः are every one of them
॰         built, all three marked `derived` in the lexicon — but a
॰         derivation made in an EMITTER is a table row written in the
॰         wrong file, which is the same objection encode.t1's blocker
॰         (a) makes about hand-copying a derived table.
॰     THE ROW THAT IS OWED: spec/registers-amd64.tsv gains rbp and rsp,
॰     marked non-allocatable so कोष्ठनाम's fourteen-arm dispatch and the
॰     `table.len() == 14` assertion in tests/t1_execution.rs both stay
॰     true, and this file reads the names from it. That file is not this
॰     row's to edit.
॰     THE MNEMONICS ARE THE SAME SHAPE OF DEBT, one size smaller: four
॰     of the five are lexicon or mnemonic-table rows read straight
॰     (स्तूपारोपः :396, स्तूपापहारः :395, योगः mnemonics:26,
॰     प्रत्यागमनम् :239) and `movq` → निधेहि is taken from the sibling
॰     emitter in this tree because no `mv` family exists in
॰     spec/mnemonics-riscv64.src.tsv. There is no spec/mnemonics-amd64
॰     .tsv at all, and if this back end grows past two instructions
॰     there needs to be one.
॰
॰ (f) CLOSED BY `W-236` (2026-09-04). It read: "कोष्ठावण्टनम् CANNOT BE RUN
॰     OVER A REAL FUNCTION … आयुर्निर्णयः asks `आयुरारम्भकोश अङ्कः मूल्यम्
॰     अन्तः समम् ०`, which is Rust's `lifetimes.get(v) == None`; a HashMap
॰     answers None for an absent key, but an arena here is grown only by
॰     WRITES … आवण्टनारम्भः clears `1..=मूल्यसीमा` and मूल्यसीमा is ० on
॰     the first call." It named two repairs and refused to make either
॰     inside an emitter row. The second one is made — आवण्टनारम्भः is told
॰     how many values मध्यरूप handed out (मध्यरूपॱअग्रिममूल्याङ्क) and
॰     clears that far — by the row whose emitter NEEDS the allocator to
॰     run, which is the row the note was waiting for. The test that
॰     asserted the refusal by name is struck as it asked to be; in its
॰     place tests/t1_execution.rs runs कोष्ठावण्टनम् over the same fixture
॰     and asserts its answer against `regalloc.rs`'s, value by value.
॰
